# API

Every error is `{ error: { code, message } }`. Zod bodies are `.strict()`. A missing or non-digit `If-Match` on PATCH is `400 invalid_body` before authorization.

A board write locks `board_launch`, increments `boards.revision` by 1, and sets the touched card version to that revision. POST `/cards`, POST `/cards/:id/comments`, and POST `/cards/:id/stars` require `Idempotency-Key`. The same key, user, and body returns the stored response with `x-keel-idempotent: replay`. The same key and a different body returns 409.

Starring does not change `boards.revision`. The first insert into `card_stars` returns 201 and emits `keel.card.starred`. A later star with a new key returns 201 and emits nothing.

Sign-up creates a member and a session. The cookie is `keel_session`. The database stores the SHA-256 hex of the token. `Secure` is set only when `KEEL_ENV=production`.

When `Origin` is present it must be `KEEL_WEB_ORIGIN` or `KEEL_STUDIO_ORIGIN`. A missing `Origin` is allowed.

New ids use a prefix plus a ULID: `card_`, `cmt_`, `ses_`, `run_`, `team_`. Migrations are `IF NOT EXISTS` files in `apps/api/migrations/`, applied on boot.
